          "final_text_tail": "that don't call `super().__init__()`\n- `add_alias(alias, target)` \u2014 stores the mapping; overwrites existing aliases; accepts any string (including `\"\"`)\n- `remove_alias(alias)` \u2014 `dict.pop(alias, None)`, safe for nonexistent names\n- `resolve_alias(template)` \u2014 single-level lookup, so aliases never chain\n- `_alias_uptodate()` / `_patch_uptodate()` \u2014 make the environment's template cache treat an alias-loaded template as out of date when the alias is removed or retargeted, so removal takes effect even in a live `Environment` (per the PR example)\n- `get_source` resolves the alias first, so all downstream `TemplateNotFound`s reference the **target** name\n\n**All subclasses** inherit the API (via `super().__init__()`) and resolve aliases at their entry points:\n- `FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader` \u2014 in `get_source`\n- `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader` \u2014 in both `get_source` and their overridden `load`\n- `ModuleLoader` \u2014 in `load` (no source access), patching `_uptodate` since `from_module_dict` sets it to `None`\n\n**Verified:** all 841 existing tests pass, plus extensive checks covering the PR's expected behavior (multiple aliases, removal on a live env, broken-alias error names, no chaining, overwrites, empty/special alias names), per-loader behavior (dict/file/package/function/choice/prefix/module, incl. `compile_templates` + `ModuleLoader`), cache identity, auto-reload, bytecode cache, async envs, `select_template`, and `{% extends %}` through aliases.",
