          "final_text_tail": "mbines both features with zero conflict markers, and all 841 existing tests pass.\n\n**Resolution strategy** \u2014 in every loader's `get_source`/`load`, alias resolution happens first, then path transformation, and `TemplateNotFound` names use the alias-resolved, untransformed name (satisfying both specs simultaneously):\n\n- `BaseLoader`: kept HEAD's `path_transform` class attr + `_transform_path()` alongside f10's `__init__`, `add_alias`/`remove_alias`/`resolve_alias`, `_alias_uptodate`/`_patch_uptodate`; `get_source` resolves aliases as in f10\n- `FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`: `name = resolve_alias(template)` \u2192 `transformed = _transform_path(name)` \u2192 `split_template_path(transformed)` wrapped in try/except re-raising with `name`; uptodate wrapped via `_alias_uptodate`\n- `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`: combined `__init__` signatures (`super().__init__()` + `path_transform` param); lookups use the transformed name, errors and alias-aware uptodate use the alias-resolved name\n- `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`: transform applied at top level before `get_loader`/child delegation; `load` tracks `original`/`name`/`transformed` and patches uptodate\n- `ModuleLoader`: unchanged (alias support only, as in f10 \u2014 path_transform wasn't part of either side for it)\n\nVerified with a 54-check functional script (both features' spec examples, error-name rules, no-chaining, cache invalidation on alias removal, exception propagation, combined alias+transform) \u2014 all passed; script removed afterward.",
